{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "5: Add the Gmail tool",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Integrate the Gmail tool with your app",
      "description": "# Integrate the Gmail tool with your app\n\nNow for the exciting part! Let's add the Gmail tool to Assistant0 so it can read and compose emails on your behalf.\n\n## Auth0 Token Vault\n\nWhen a user prompt requires the agent to use the Gmail tool, the user be redirected to grant permission on the required scopes. Auth0 will then securely store the necessary tokens (access and refresh tokens) in the [Token Vault](https://auth0.com/docs/secure/tokens/token-vault).\n\nOur AI agent, through the Auth0 AI SDK, will then request these tokens from Auth0 to make authenticated API calls to Gmail on the user's behalf. This keeps sensitive credentials out of our application code and gives users control over what the agent can access.",
      "type": "markdown"
    },
    {
      "file": "auth0-assistant0/src/lib/auth0-ai.ts",
      "description": "## Import functions from Auth0 AI SDK and helper function\n\n**Notice that `auth0-ai.ts` has been opened for you above. We will add some code in this step.**\n\nFirst, we need to get an access token for the Gmail API. We can get this using the Auth0 Token Vault.\n\n1. Import the `Auth0AI` constructor and the `getAccessTokenFromTokenVault` functions from the Auth0 AI SDK and our `getRefreshToken` function from `./auth0.js` by selecting the **Insert code** button below:\n\n\n```ts\nimport { Auth0AI, getAccessTokenFromTokenVault } from '@auth0/ai-vercel';\nimport { getRefreshToken } from './auth0.js';\n```\n",
      "line": 3,
      "title": "Import functions from Auth0 AI SDK and helper function",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 2,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 2,
          "character": 34
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "auth0-assistant0/src/lib/auth0-ai.ts",
      "description": "## Get an access token for a connection\n\n**Notice that `auth0-ai.ts` has been opened for you above. We will add some code in this step.**\n\n1. Next, we'll export a helper that retrieves the Google access token stored by the Token Vault during tool execution. Select **Insert Code** to add this code:\n\n```ts\nexport const getAccessToken = getAccessTokenFromTokenVault;\n```\n\n> Note: We'll still need to specify which connection we are requesting a token from. We will do that next!\n",
      "line": 12,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 12,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 12,
          "character": 36
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "auth0-assistant0/src/lib/auth0-ai.ts",
      "description": "## Initialize the Auth0 AI client and Google Connection for Token Vault\n\n**Notice that `auth0-ai.ts` has been opened for you above. We will add some code in this step.**\n\n1. Next, we'll initialize a new Auth0AI client and specify the connection with Google so the Auth0 AI SDK can request tokens from Token Vault. Notice that the scopes are the ones that will allow the agent to read and compose emails. Select the **Insert Code** below to add this code segment to the agent code:\n\n```ts\n// Initialize Auth0AI client\nconst auth0AI = new Auth0AI();\n\n// Connection for Google services\nexport const withGmailRead = auth0AI.withTokenVault({\n  connection: 'google-oauth2',\n  scopes: ['openid', 'https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly'],\n  refreshToken: getRefreshToken,\n});\nexport const withGmailWrite = auth0AI.withTokenVault({\n  connection: 'google-oauth2',\n  scopes: ['openid', 'https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.compose'],\n  refreshToken: getRefreshToken,\n});\n```\n",
      "line": 27,
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 14,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 14,
          "character": 81
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "auth0-assistant0/src/app.ts",
      "description": "## Import the Gmail tools\n\n**Notice that the Express app code in `src/app.ts` has been opened for you above. We will add some code in this step.**\n\nIn order to implement Gmail tool-calling, we'll need to import the Gmail tools.\n\n1. Import the Gmail tools with the code below by selecting **Insert Code**.\n\n```ts\nimport { gmailSearchTool, gmailComposeTool } from './tools/gmail.js';\n```\n\n> The `gmailComposeTool` is used to send email while `gmailSearchTool` is used to search and read emails from your inbox.",
      "line": 17,
      "title": "Import the Gmail tools",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 17,
          "character": 1
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 17,
          "character": 33
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "file": "auth0-assistant0/src/app.ts",
      "description": "## Update the list of tools\n\n1. Now we need to add our Gmail tools to the `streamText` call. Currently the tools object is empty so let's replace that code with the snippet below by selecting **Insert Code** below:\n\n```ts\n      tools: { gmailSearch: gmailSearchTool, gmailCompose: gmailComposeTool },\n```\n",
      "line": 321,
      "title": "Update the list of tools",
      "selection": {
